unction $f(x)=5(x+1)^{2}+8.$\n\n{{field-1}}\n$\\le f(x)$\n{{field-2}}{{field-3}}" :question/worked-solution "The parabola is written in vertex form, \n\n$$\ny=a(x-h)^{2}+k,\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ is the leading coefficient and $(h,k)$ is the vertex.\n\n- Since $h=-1$ and $k=8,$ the vertex is $(-1,8).$\n\n- Since $a=5>0,$ the parabola opens upwards.\n\nBecause the parabola opens upwards, there is no maximum output, and the vertex corresponds to the minimum output.\n\nTherefore, the range is $[8,\\infty ),$ i.e. $8\\le f(x)<\\infty .$\n\nThe corresponding diagram is shown below.\n\n![](images/7f/7ff6f49b63c4ad55324bbb406558781c9f3e5af3a98d34b285c65f88746bddab.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186562408 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124584 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "56d457de-8511-5870-98e3-b81e72e60585" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Range of a Parabola Given in Vertex Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "80ef7f3f-43e2-5afc-b357-efcbd63dcaec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\infty" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561904}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "80ef7f3f-43e2-5afc-b357-efcbd63dcaec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\infty" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561904} :answer-field/id #uuid "56f50417-a8db-5569-b297-00307ac7e3ed" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562277} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f0a5d71b-22b4-5f8a-b763-aa7e35f62c9f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "<" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562180}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f0a5d71b-22b4-5f8a-b763-aa7e35f62c9f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "<" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562180} :answer-field/id #uuid "e90fc8d9-ab85-53eb-b3c7-0a25c8c47225" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562371} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e9317a34-9fc1-5c7d-a546-fec08a118649" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562160}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e9317a34-9fc1-5c7d-a546-fec08a118649" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562160} :answer-field/id #uuid "fa3565a8-730f-5135-b58e-5e5914abff83" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562380}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "2002fa84-a05e-5e54-ad18-933be8248d10" :question/math-academy-id "q-250607" :question/problem "Find the range of the function $f(x)=-3(x+5)^{2}+7.$\n\n{{field-1}}{{field-2}}\n$f(x)\\le $\n{{field-3}}" :question/worked-solution "The parabola is written in vertex form, \n\n$$\ny=a(x-h)^{2}+k,\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ is the leading coefficient and $(h,k)$ is the vertex. \n\n- Since $h=-5$ and $k=7,$ the vertex is $(-5,7).$\n\n- Since $a=-3<0,$ the parabola opens downwards.\n\nBecause the parabola opens downwards, there is no minimum output, and the vertex corresponds to the maximum output.\n\nTherefore, the range is $(-\\infty ,7],$ i.e. $-\\infty <f(x)\\le 7.$\n\nThe corresponding diagram is shown below.\n\n![](images/25/252a3c0475f838b1835f2da9c3c818a938c916b781c5abaa1f12ed09c52c56f6.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186562437 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124659 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b1bc2396-f949-57a0-be50-d5606abe3372" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Range of a Parabola Given in Standard Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c9125bed-e59b-5820-bb19-1b272efd5b76" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\infty" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562082}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c9125bed-e59b-5820-bb19-1b272efd5b76" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\infty" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562082} :answer-field/id #uuid "09ce1543-bab3-5287-8403-e2b7bf000729" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562225} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3b8db516-3ec3-52ed-bcd3-204a1eac8e73" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561730}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3b8db516-3ec3-52ed-bcd3-204a1eac8e73" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561730} :answer-field/id #uuid "2ea59e43-3e9e-551b-b8f4-d4b59960c0d1" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562249} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "17a85056-0a28-50b2-a9dc-d58df89de9a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "<" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561651}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "17a85056-0a28-50b2-a9dc-d58df89de9a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "<" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561651} :answer-field/id #uuid "3cb67adb-362a-502d-ba97-5bf0f0b88ad1" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562261}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "5e73f5fc-13ec-5727-bb90-2579fb0880d6" :question/math-academy-id "q-250633" :question/problem "Find the range of the function $f(x)=2{x}^{2}+8x+11.$\n\n{{field-1}}\n$\\le f(x)$\n{{field-2}}{{field-3}}" :question/worked-solution "The given parabola is written in standard form,\n\n$$\ny=a{x}^{2}+bx+c,\n$$\n\nwith $a=2>0,$ $b=8,$ and $c=11.$\n\nBecause the leading coefficient is positive, the parabola opens upward. Consequently, there is no maximum output, and the vertex corresponds to the minimum output.\n\nThe $x$-coordinate of the vertex is given by\n\n$$\nx=-\\frac{b}{2a}=-\\frac{8}{2\\cdot 2}=-2.\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute $x=-2$ back into the function to find the $y$-value of the vertex:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =2{x}^{2}+8x+11 \\\\  & =2(-2)^{2}+8(-2)+11 \\\\  & =8-16+11 \\\\  & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the vertex is $(-2,3),$ and the range of the function is $[3,\\infty ),$ i.e. $3\\le f(x)<\\infty .$\n\n![](images/3a/3a87830f59bf840ac8ab0d761ab7319b53fc804bc9d925e92850313d5d5a7a52.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186562458 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124659 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b1bc2396-f949-57a0-be50-d5606abe3372" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Range of a Parabola Given in Standard Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6431dec3-2744-5c91-9888-35fb8d486a49" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\le" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561827}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6431dec3-2744-5c91-9888-35fb8d486a49" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\le" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561827} :answer-field/id #uuid "788caaeb-874f-5a58-a638-27770e22a12b" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562301} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "560383cf-7bf3-5f2c-8cdd-a33f83f8439c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\infty" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561795}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "560383cf-7bf3-5f2c-8cdd-a33f83f8439c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\infty" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561795} :answer-field/id #uuid "8e23828e-dbe8-55aa-ba5d-1021ce14ba4b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562315} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "35735545-6764-5af4-8b30-c44340961668" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561719}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "35735545-6764-5af4-8b30-c44340961668" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561719} :answer-field/id #uuid "c1c47709-4fb4-5410-8bb2-077d0d2f6c96" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562346}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "89ea5a4a-e490-551f-988c-728a0c124eab" :question/math-academy-id "q-250639" :question/problem "Find the range of the function $f(x)=-{x}^{2}+4x+1.$\n\n{{field-1}}\n$<f(x)$\n{{field-2}}{{field-3}}" :question/worked-solution "The given parabola is written in standard form,\n\n$$\ny=a{x}^{2}+bx+c,\n$$\n\nwith $a=-1<0,$ $b=4,$ and $c=1.$\n\nBecause the leading coefficient is negative, the parabola opens downward. Consequently, there is no minimum output, and the vertex corresponds to the maximum output.\n\nThe $x$-coordinate of the vertex is given by\n\n$$\nx=-\\frac{b}{2a}=-\\frac{4}{2\\cdot (-1)}=2.\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute $x=2$ back into the function to find the $y$-value of the vertex:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =-{x}^{2}+4x+1 \\\\  & =-(2)^{2}+4(2)+1 \\\\  & =-4+8+1 \\\\  & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the vertex is $(2,5),$ and the range of the function is $(-\\infty ,5],$ i.e. $-\\infty <f(x)\\le 5.$\n\n![](images/ce/ce52355662b526af83614a6c4cbe6e7f2d7f07d379b2636d14e094d47e0e0da6.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186562459 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124660 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fb0d6e0e-bf61-5fe9-bf8a-ab15c5846e11" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Range of a Parabola Given in Factored Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "78afb764-e323-511a-a2f2-0a8264faacfd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561881}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "78afb764-e323-511a-a2f2-0a8264faacfd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561881} :answer-field/id #uuid "453c5296-23d3-57ab-bead-b0c23a1b99d7" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562268} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6c978228-4f12-5690-9c85-cedfcd98d83e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\infty" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561852}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6c978228-4f12-5690-9c85-cedfcd98d83e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\infty" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561852} :answer-field/id #uuid "7323c510-56c5-5c7a-8032-b64a15edc529" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562295} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6a2fff73-ed51-5034-b645-c0efebc9c710" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\le" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561849}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6a2fff73-ed51-5034-b645-c0efebc9c710" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\le" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561849} :answer-field/id #uuid "cf3e671d-1011-5362-908e-3f28855f4af3" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562353}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8a31f28b-9e61-5b12-8422-c1bd2c17fb23" :question/math-academy-id "q-250644" :question/problem "Find the range of the function $f(x)=(x-2)(x-8).$\n\n{{field-1}}{{field-2}}\n$f(x)<$\n{{field-3}}" :question/worked-solution "The given parabola is written in factored form,\n\n$$\ny=a(x-{x}_{1})(x-{x}_{2}),\n$$\n\nwith $a=1>0.$ \n\nBecause the leading coefficient is positive, the parabola opens upward. Consequently, there is no maximum output, and the vertex corresponds to the minimum output.\n\nThe two roots of the parabola are ${x}_{1}=2$ and ${x}_{2}=8,$ and we can find the $x$-coordinate of the vertex by taking the average of the roots:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\frac{{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}}{2}=\\frac{2+8}{2}=5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute $x=5$ back into the function to find the $y$-value of the vertex:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =(x-2)(x-8) \\\\  & =(5-2)(5-8) \\\\  & =3\\cdot (-3) \\\\  & =-9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the vertex is $(5,-9),$ and the range of the function is $[-9,\\infty ),$ i.e. $-9\\le f(x)<\\infty .$\n\n![](images/84/84c22aee72ebd52e3dab84a72ad1d402813c3a38794c653cd4cb0e31bfef3836.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186562517 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124660 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fb0d6e0e-bf61-5fe9-bf8a-ab15c5846e11" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Range of a Parabola Given in Factored Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a4df160b-dd1f-5ade-944d-c37298bccec1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 