\frac{1}{5}(x+9)(x-1).$\n\n{{field-1}}\n$\\le f(x)$\n{{field-2}}{{field-3}}" :question/worked-solution "The given parabola is written in factored form,\n\n$$\ny=a(x-{x}_{1})(x-{x}_{2}),\n$$\n\nwith $a=\\frac{1}{5}>0.$ \n\nBecause the leading coefficient is positive, the parabola opens upward. Consequently, there is no maximum output, and the vertex corresponds to the minimum output.\n\nThe two roots of the parabola are ${x}_{1}=-9$ and ${x}_{2}=1,$ and we can find the $x$-coordinate of the vertex by taking the average of the roots:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\frac{{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}}{2}=\\frac{-9+1}{2}=-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute $x=-4$ back into the function to find the $y$-value of the vertex:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\frac{1}{5}(x+9)(x-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}(-4+9)(-4-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}\\cdot 5\\cdot (-5) \\\\  & =-5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the vertex is $(-4,-5),$ and the range of the function is $[-5,\\infty ),$ i.e. $-5\\le f(x)<\\infty .$\n\n![](images/97/97c587abebf09ff27a805db3b32b3c5f26b5d51baaf7f6827618e01ccdd53642.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186562462 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124660 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fb0d6e0e-bf61-5fe9-bf8a-ab15c5846e11" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Range of a Parabola Given in Factored Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3c44ff17-61f3-54f4-b363-ea1bd3f109e0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "<" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561731}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3c44ff17-61f3-54f4-b363-ea1bd3f109e0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "<" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561731} :answer-field/id #uuid "35f138a0-b129-5c92-b044-9a7f9862134f" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562254} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "27679f0a-767b-58cd-8144-921030108067" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561688}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "27679f0a-767b-58cd-8144-921030108067" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561688} :answer-field/id #uuid "3cb408db-786a-5b26-a5af-0f25b4b11d35" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562260} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cf0f59aa-7331-50e4-b1d5-d86e0389fe30" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\infty" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562098}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cf0f59aa-7331-50e4-b1d5-d86e0389fe30" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\infty" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562098} :answer-field/id #uuid "e7e6e4e4-ba72-5524-86c2-1327a0ed5696" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562369}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8f69a422-81e0-551f-abc6-71d3ea93c826" :question/math-academy-id "q-250649" :question/problem "Find the range of the function $f(x)=-4(x-1)(x-4).$\n\n{{field-1}}{{field-2}}\n$f(x)\\le $\n{{field-3}}" :question/worked-solution "The given parabola is written in factored form,\n\n$$\ny=a(x-{x}_{1})(x-{x}_{2}),\n$$\n\nwith $a=-4<0.$ \n\nBecause the leading coefficient is negative, the parabola opens downward. Consequently, there is no minimum output, and the vertex corresponds to the maximum output.\n\nThe two roots of the parabola are ${x}_{1}=1$ and ${x}_{2}=4,$ and we can find the $x$-coordinate of the vertex by taking the average of the roots:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\frac{{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}}{2}=\\frac{1+4}{2}=\\frac{5}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute $x=\\frac{5}{2}$ back into the function to find the $y$-value of the vertex:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =-4(x-1)(x-4) \\\\  & =-4(\\frac{5}{2}-1)(\\frac{5}{2}-4) \\\\  & =-4\\cdot \\frac{3}{2}\\cdot (-\\frac{3}{2}) \\\\  & =9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the vertex is $(\\frac{5}{2},9),$ and the range of the function is $(-\\infty ,9],$ i.e. $-\\infty <f(x)\\le 9.$\n\n![](images/70/70dc863f5f089c9434d783495c31b77fd7a0ac84a852d2b32222b445f463efe3.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124866 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124584 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "56d457de-8511-5870-98e3-b81e72e60585" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Range of a Parabola Given in Vertex Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "25995585-8181-58ec-9ca2-df6919080cd3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-\\infty ,\\frac{5}{6}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561684} {:answer/id #uuid "4e47ff5f-6b08-5d07-a62a-c241fb59bdf0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-\\infty ,-\\frac{1}{2}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561782} {:answer/id #uuid "a19b54fd-b859-58ec-9f48-c6622db47056" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[-\\frac{1}{2},\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561984} {:answer/id #uuid "b8a8d8b1-1116-562c-9eac-92b96751313a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-\\frac{1}{2},\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562049} {:answer/id #uuid "e364e522-0636-5c3f-b534-a21b5528a7bf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[-\\frac{5}{6},\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562142}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a19b54fd-b859-58ec-9f48-c6622db47056" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[-\\frac{1}{2},\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561984} :answer-field/id #uuid "600d4fe3-3e54-5f82-b63d-17a852bf35e0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186121796}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1930d180-4cc3-5e28-910d-7be8bef132f9" :question/math-academy-id "q-34886" :question/problem "What is the range of the function $f(x)={(x+\\frac{5}{6})}^{2}-\\frac{1}{2}?$" :question/worked-solution "The parabola is written in vertex form, \n\n$$\ny=a(x-h)^{2}+k,\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ is the leading coefficient and $(h,k)$ is the vertex. \n\n- Since $h=-\\frac{5}{6}$ and $k=-\\frac{1}{2},$ the vertex is $(-\\frac{5}{6},-\\frac{1}{2}).$\n\n- Since $a=1>0,$ the parabola opens upwards.\n\nBecause the parabola opens upwards, there is no maximum output, and the vertex corresponds to the minimum output.\n\nTherefore, the range is $[-\\frac{1}{2},\\infty ).$ \n\n![](images/54/54e0b0ea5dd498a36fc854781dc5120ce1de9bee0c333eecc6d895ce09b72424.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186549928 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124584 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "56d457de-8511-5870-98e3-b81e72e60585" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Range of a Parabola Given in Vertex Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "17490e92-f04a-51f7-b438-199eeb712801" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[0,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186549361} {:answer/id #uuid "8e98df84-9ac6-56f7-ab33-a824ee4007cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186549593} {:answer/id #uuid "c5d59e6e-34b2-5e9c-b08e-8f2105c0bb6e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-\\infty ,3]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186549686} {:answer/id #uuid "ec8b8a2d-5b31-5cfd-aa2c-e0f8c2791516" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[-3,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186549751} {:answer/id #uuid "f856d9c9-25b2-55b1-83a5-4041c1afdc91" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[3,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186549782}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ec8b8a2d-5b31-5cfd-aa2c-e0f8c2791516" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[-3,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186549751} :answer-field/id #uuid "d506de6d-4e6d-5568-a53f-79ffc50374e1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186549902}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0bc8d353-4f35-531e-9326-d4dcbc01bbdb" :question/math-academy-id "q-35908" :question/problem "What is the range of the function $y=f(x)=(x-1)^{2}-3?$" :question/worked-solution "The parabola is written in vertex form, \n\n$$\ny=a(x-h)^{2}+k,\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ is the leading coefficient and $(h,k)$ is the vertex. \n\n- Since $h=1$ and $k=-3,$ the vertex is $(1,-3).$\n\n- Since $a=1>0,$ the parabola opens upwards.\n\nBecause the parabola opens upwards, there is no maximum output, and the vertex corresponds to the minimum output. \n\nTherefore, the range is $[-3,\\infty ).$\n\nThe corresponding diagram is shown below.\n\n![](images/26/265532f4f4726151444ed873b875fc62c3c32a690a0ac859a318e2d4dc8fd285.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124930 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124583 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "713fb1a0-5d7b-5cde-aafe-de5887086e1b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Domain of a Quadratic Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "108b871c-1da3-5a28-94d4-955f