of a Parabola Given in Standard Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "81c5bbf2-cb3f-5027-93c7-adfd59d8054d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-\\infty ,3]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561906} {:answer/id #uuid "abd657a4-c200-5733-9a0a-52aadbe8c41c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562009} {:answer/id #uuid "ba14fcfa-ffa6-571d-88a3-f4da05a8b41d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-\\infty ,5]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562057} {:answer/id #uuid "e6a97956-8fdf-547f-bcc6-039d7a0099a2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[3,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562149} {:answer/id #uuid "f39445c2-f0a2-5251-85ea-f5894b6372ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[5,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562188}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e6a97956-8fdf-547f-bcc6-039d7a0099a2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[3,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562149} :answer-field/id #uuid "9c8213d1-9456-5a4c-8f8c-8fb8f595c764" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186124022}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8151bd28-84e4-5d59-ba0b-4c6824e316e3" :question/math-academy-id "q-90776" :question/problem "What is the range of the function $f(x)=2{x}^{2}-4x+5?$" :question/worked-solution "The given parabola is written in standard form,\n\n$$\ny=a{x}^{2}+bx+c,\n$$\n\nwith $a=2>0,$ $b=-4,$ and $c=5.$\n\nBecause the leading coefficient is positive, the parabola opens upward. Consequently, there is no maximum output, and the vertex corresponds to the minimum output.\n\nThe $x$-coordinate of the vertex is given by\n\n$$\nx=-\\frac{b}{2a}=-\\frac{(-4)}{2\\cdot 2}=1.\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute $x=1$ back into the function to find the $y$-value of the vertex:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =2{x}^{2}-4x+5 \\\\  & =2(1)^{2}-4(1)+5 \\\\  & =2-4+5 \\\\  & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the vertex is $(1,3),$ and the range of the function is $[3,\\infty ).$\n\n![](images/a8/a8fc15df2b24054485bb07330f40919ebf13cb9969073a733b9426a28dab20b5.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186562401 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124583 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "713fb1a0-5d7b-5cde-aafe-de5887086e1b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Domain of a Quadratic Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "24d5f16b-6c16-5c94-b175-7613bdb3bca3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\in (-1,3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561680} {:answer/id #uuid "2a54822c-590b-5c91-a4d1-72c3a33134f7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\in (-\\infty ,-4)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561693} {:answer/id #uuid "3d6ea30a-6482-5618-8571-d8bc24a1deab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\in (-\\infty ,-1)\\cup (3,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561734} {:answer/id #uuid "5782c08a-0200-5db4-8c8b-e24306102b43" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\in (-4,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561797} {:answer/id #uuid "cd0e70c7-01be-51d3-a5db-399e47a17da0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562092}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cd0e70c7-01be-51d3-a5db-399e47a17da0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\in (-\\infty